---
interface Props { projectType?: 'all' | 'website' | 'automation' }
const { projectType = 'all' } = Astro.props;
const automationOnly = projectType === 'automation';
---

<section id="project-planning" class="section project-planning" aria-labelledby="planning-heading">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <h2 id="planning-heading">Timing & your part.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="planning-overview">
    <div>
      <h3>About 1–2 weeks</h3>
      <p>{automationOnly
        ? 'For a small, defined workflow. I confirm timing after reviewing your tools and sample data.'
        : 'For a small website, from our agreed start once content and access are ready.'}</p>
      {projectType === 'all' && <p>Automation timing depends on the workflow and tools.</p>}
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>{automationOnly ? 'Try an early version' : 'A first look in 1–2 days'}</h3>
      <p>{automationOnly
        ? 'Review a working version, refine it, and check the agreed test cases before handover.'
        : 'I aim for a first draft in 1–2 business days for straightforward sites, then revisions and final checks.'}</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Your part</h3>
      <p>Share your goals and materials, send one feedback list per revision round, and give final approval. Rough notes are fine to start.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="schedule-note">Your quote confirms scope, revisions, price, payment terms, and dates. Larger projects, missing materials, or slower feedback can extend these estimates.</p>
  <div class:list={['preparation-grid', { 'single-project': projectType !== 'all' }]}>
    {projectType !== 'automation' && (
      <details class="preparation-card">
        <summary>What to provide for a website</summary>
        <ul>
          <li>Your business, audience, services, and the action visitors should take.</li>
          <li>A few websites you like and why.</li>
          <li>Draft text, plus any existing logo, colors, photos, or videos.</li>
          <li>Your current website, domain, and hosting details.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Missing materials? We’ll agree how to handle them and quote any extra work.</p>
      </details>
    )}
    {projectType !== 'website' && (
      <details class="preparation-card">
        <summary>What to provide for automation</summary>
        <ul>
          <li>The repeated task, its steps, frequency, and bottlenecks.</li>
          <li>Your apps or spreadsheets and what needs to move between them.</li>
          <li>Samples with private details removed, the desired result, and exceptions.</li>
          <li>Who uses the result and who can arrange tool access.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>A walkthrough or screenshots help. We agree access and test cases during planning.</p>
      </details>
    )}
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .project-planning .section-heading { align-items: start; }
  .planning-overview { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 32px; }
  .planning-overview h3 { font-size: 1.3rem; }
  .planning-overview p, .preparation-card p, .preparation-card li { color: var(--muted); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.8; }
  .planning-overview p { margin-top: 14px; }
  .schedule-note { max-width: 90ch; margin-top: 24px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.7; }
  .preparation-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); align-items: start; margin-top: 28px; gap: 16px; }
  .preparation-card { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 16px; background: var(--paper); overflow: hidden; }
  .preparation-card:first-child { background: #eef2dc; }
  .preparation-card summary { padding: 20px 24px; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; }
  .preparation-card summary:focus-visible { outline-offset: -5px; }
  .preparation-card ul { list-style: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin: 0 24px 18px; }
  .preparation-card li + li { margin-top: 10px; }
  .preparation-card > p { margin: 0 24px 24px; font-size: 13px; }
  .single-project { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
  .single-project .preparation-card ul { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 14px 40px; }
  .single-project .preparation-card li + li { margin-top: 0; }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .planning-overview, .preparation-grid, .single-project .preparation-card ul { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
  }
</style>
